<title>FRANCE: Algeria's Zeralda tourism firm loses 17 mln dinars.</title>
<headline>Algeria's Zeralda tourism firm loses 17 mln dinars.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state-owned Zeralda tourist firm, Entreprise de Gestion du Centre Touristique de Zeralda (EGCT), made a 17.28 million dinars ($308,520) loss in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Thursday.</p>
<p>EGCT, which owns several hotels and tourist assets in the Mediterranean coastal resort, southwest of Algiers, posted 1.2 billion dinars ($21.7 million) turnover in 1995, said APS.</p>
<p>There were no figures for 1996 or comparative data available.</p>
<p>($ = 56 dinars)</p>
</text>
